+#!/usr/bin/env node
+/**
+ * check-peer-arcs — THE PLAYER'S HUE IS NOT ALLOWED TO BE A COLOUR THE HOUSE ALREADY SPENT.
+ *
+ * `playerIdentity.ts` walks a golden step over the arcs of the wheel `index.css` has NOT
+ * reserved, so that no hand at the table is ever mistakable for a crayon, an ink tier, the
+ * solver's rainbow or the local blue. The arcs are a CONSTANT in that file because a browser
+ * cannot read a stylesheet's source at run time — which means the constant and the stylesheet
+ * are two statements of one fact, and two statements of one fact drift.
+ *
+ * EVERY STYLESHEET AND EVERY SOURCE IS READ THROUGH THE ESTATE'S ONE SHAPE LIBRARY
+ * (`./shape-census.mjs`, registry-v7 §2.4; LAWS P7 §F (i)). This file carries no reader of its
+ * own: the rules and their at-rule context, the `@import` chain, every site a custom property is
+ * declared at (a rule, a `style=""`, a `:style` key, a `setProperty`, a `cssText` or
+ * `setAttribute("style", …)` write with its concatenation folded, a Tailwind arbitrary property, a
+ * `.json` key) and every colour literal come from the library. The fork this file carried through
+ * pass 7 missed four shapes the library reads (a concatenated `cssText`, a concatenated
+ * `setAttribute`, a computed `:style` key, an `@import`ed sheet outside `src/`) — it is deleted.
+ *
+ *   1  ARCS AGREE     the arcs derived from index.css == RESERVED_ARCS. Reserved is found by
+ *                     RESOLVED VALUE (aliases followed, any colour syntax), never by a name.
+ *   2  THE SEPARATION LAW  (PAL-TIN's whole law, registry-v7 §2.13b, handed by sha c8c129f7) the
+ *                     digit, the ring and the name of the hands a session has ISSUED, as the
+ *                     engine paints them (8-bit), no two closer than MIN_DE in OKLab (the day ring
+ *                     at RING_FLOOR), both arms, over EVERY PAIR — an index is never reassigned, so
+ *                     a room of two after any churn is any pair of the issued hands, never the
+ *                     first two. The walk holds it for SEP_HANDS = 2 issued hands (the claim is
+ *                     gated: a capacity that moves reds); TIN's room of five and the churned
+ *                     rooms of 8 and 16 are printed beside HEAD's one string every run, and the
+ *                     cost the B-TAPE row writes down for 8 and 16 is GATED as written (CHURN_COST).
+ *                     The decoy (the complement is open, the step repeats no hue) stays a
+ *                     precondition, each with its own switch.
+ *   3  BANDS AGREE    `DIGIT_BANDS` / `RING_BANDS` / `NAME_BANDS` == the `--peer-ink-l` /
+ *                     `--peer-ring-l` / `--peer-name-l` the sheet publishes, per arm, and each
+ *                     string is bisected against its own table. THE CI PIN (LAWS P7 §F): the
+ *                     name's night band is ≥ NAME_FLOOR on BOTH sides (the basis is NAME_FLOOR's
+ *                     own note), so a coordinated move of module and sheet to 0.83 reds here, not
+ *                     only in the local paint gate.
+ *   4  ONE PUBLISHER  every declaration of a band or a player's ink, anywhere the library reads
+ *                     (src/ with its tests, e2e/, public/**, index.html, every @import), sits at
+ *                     an admitted site bound to its own value, or reds; a templated or computed
+ *                     name reds; a lightness under a band-shaped name, a hex table under a
+ *                     player-shaped name, a colour literal within ΔE 0.02 of a walked ink and a
+ *                     Tailwind candidate for a band or an ink each red.
+ *   5  THE PAIR       (r0 law L6's pair half, LANDED — registry-v7 §2.13i) over index.css AND
+ *                     every sheet it `@import`s: each band var has exactly one light arm
+ *                     (`:root`/`@theme`, top level) and one dark arm (`.dark`, top level) in
+ *                     index.css and none elsewhere; the ring arms sit at the §2.4 pair
+ *                     (0.295 / 0.79), the name's day arm IS the ring's and its night arm ≥
+ *                     NAME_FLOOR; `--color-user-ink` has only the house's three literal arms
+ *                     and no peer ink token is declared in any sheet of the chain.
